A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate when evidence supports the **same cause**, under
[decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause). This replaces the subject-only rule in
[historical decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).

1. Deduplicate overlapping export rows by report ID.
2. Look up the tenant's locale and booking form, and check the report channel.
3. Use `causeOf` and compare mechanisms with `sameCause`; inspect the body for contradictions.
4. Merge only supported same-cause reports. Different or unknown causes stay apart.
5. Keep engineering tickets, computed counts and the rendered KB current as reports arrive.

<Callout>
Subjects help find reports; they do not establish duplicate causes. Intake tags and browser
locales are guesses. See the [review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review).
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep it apart for review. Record what is missing or contradictory. Do not turn uncertainty
into a confirmed root cause or hide it in a known ticket.

